  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased use of monitoring and evaluation information for RBM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By systematically integrating M&amp;E data into decision-making processes, the ILO Regional Office for Africa can enhance oversight mechanisms, ensuring that organizational leadership and governance are evidence-driven, transparent, and accountable.
While monitoring and evaluation efforts exist, systematic integration into decision-making remains inconsistent. Challenges include:
     - Variability in the timeliness and quality of evaluations, affecting their usability.
     - Limited implementation rates of evaluation recommendations, reducing learning impact.
     - Limited alignment of M&amp;E with organizational learning needs, leading to missed opportunities for improvement.
This Regional Outcome aims to achieve:
     - Institutional Change &#x2013; Strengthening ILO&#x2019;s internal M&amp;E systems, ensuring that evaluation findings inform leadership and governance decisions at all levels.
     - Behavioral Change &#x2013; Encouraging ILO leadership and project managers to proactively use evaluation insights for policy formulation, risk management, and strategic adjustments.
     - Transparency &amp; Accountability &#x2013; Improving the timeliness of evaluations and enhancing implementation rates of recommendations to ensure tangible improvements in programme effectiveness.
This work contributes to the advancement of ILO&#x2019;s cross-cutting policy drivers by:
     - International Labour Standards (ILS): Strengthening M&amp;E integration ensures that ILO programmes align with and promote compliance with ILS through better impact assessment.
     - Gender Equality &amp; Non-Discrimination: Encouraging sex-disaggregated data collection and gender-responsive evaluation methodologies to ensure that policies and programmes are inclusive.
     - Social Dialogue: Ensuring that evaluation findings are shared with tripartite constituents to inform policy discussions and decision-making processes.
     - Just Transition &amp; Environmental Sustainability: Embedding sustainability indicators into M&amp;E practices to as</narrative>
  </description>
